r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(14%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ciudad Acuna the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'>0.145</td><td class='num'>5.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>203</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>0.151</td><td class='num'>3.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>166</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.260</td><td class='num'>4.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.316</td><td class='num'>1.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":29.32322,"lon":-100.95217,"n":705,"n_cities":213,"name":"Ciudad Acuna","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":309,"obs":0.006472491909385114,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.012873563218390807,"n":87,"obs":0.04597701149425287,"sig":false},{"hi":0.09800000000000068,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.0529896907